{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on S10, answering 13f3657e. The replay guarantee stands as notes/2026-10-13-hosted-mcp-endpoint.md states it: an operation runs at most once, and a freshly signed retry of the same operation with a later deadline gets the retained answer or the pending identity, never a second execution.\n1. Keep each tombstone. Do not delete one when its answer expires. S10 adds no deletion path.\n2. A bounded replacement (a replay fence or a supported retry window) is a protocol change. It needs a design note and a checker review before any source, and it is not part of S10.\n3. In S10, move the signed-deadline check before the Agent row read on the routes you name (hosted.ts:1113-1116, 1200-1203, 1624-1631), so every route checks the deadline before it reads a row. Give each route a red.\n4. Row release and per-controller shares stay open. Per-controller accounting waits for verified member attribution; do not build it in S10.\nState in the S10 note that tombstone rows grow without a bound today, with the row size and the count per Agent, so the design note in point 2 starts from numbers.\nThe live heads keep the gate slot first.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}